# Keeps the harness image's build context (repo root) small and
# deterministic. Only `harness/two-principal/Dockerfile` uses a context
# wider than its own directory today, but `.dockerignore` applies
# wherever `docker build` is invoked from this root, so this file is
# written generally rather than scoped to one Dockerfile.
/target
/target-*
.git
.DS_Store
/experiments
/site/book
